WEBVTT

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:08.235
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1

00:00:09.273 --> 00:00:12.405
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> We’ve decided <b>to go</b> to France for our holiday.

00:00:14.394 --> 00:00:15.084
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

00:00:16.131 --> 00:00:18.459
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Don’t forget <b>to turn off</b> all the lights.

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:21.331
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3

00:00:22.383 --> 00:00:24.387
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> We hope <b>to see</b> you again soon.

00:00:26.447 --> 00:00:27.146
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 4

00:00:28.185 --> 00:00:29.916
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> I’m learning <b>to drive</b>.

00:00:30.393 --> 00:00:32.233
My test is next month.

00:00:34.272 --> 00:00:35.107
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 5

00:00:36.125 --> 00:00:38.627
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> I need <b>to go</b> to the supermarket.

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:40.258
I don’t have any milk.

00:00:42.325 --> 00:00:43.123
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 6

00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:46.301
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> He offered <b>to help</b> me with my CV.

00:00:48.253 --> 00:00:49.056
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 7

00:00:50.004 --> 00:00:52.024
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> They’re planning <b>to get married</b> this summer.

00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:54.699
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 8

00:00:55.666 --> 00:00:58.964
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> He pretended <b>to be</b> ill, but he wasn’t really.

00:01:01.019 --> 00:01:01.764
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 9

00:01:02.826 --> 00:01:05.688
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> He’s promised <b>to pay</b> me back when he gets a job.

00:01:07.723 --> 00:01:08.322
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 10

00:01:09.443 --> 00:01:13.056
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Remember <b>to bring</b> your dictionaries to class tomorrow.

00:01:15.094 --> 00:01:15.895
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 11

00:01:16.878 --> 00:01:20.124
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> It was very cloudy and it started <b>to rain</b>.

00:01:22.195 --> 00:01:22.993
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 12

00:01:23.985 --> 00:01:27.461
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> I’m trying <b>to find</b> a job, but it’s very hard.

00:01:29.516 --> 00:01:30.422
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 13

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:34.330
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> I want <b>to catch</b> the six o’clock train.

00:01:36.422 --> 00:01:37.357
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 14

00:01:38.436 --> 00:01:40.930
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> I’d like <b>to buy</b> a new car next month.